Microsoft API documentation, CC BY 4.0 (export name lists)
----------------------------------------------------------

src/exports/{kernel32,ntdll,user32,advapi32}.txt list the export names the
synthetic system DLLs advertise. scripts/gen-exports.py, in this crate,
extracts them from the metadata of Microsoft's API reference pages: for each
page marked as a DLL export, the function name and the DLLs that export it.
Nothing else from the pages is used. The lists are a selection and
rearrangement of that metadata (names only, sorted, one per line). One name is
added by the script with its reason stated there: ntdll's RtlDecompressBuffer,
which the documentation records only under NtosKrnl.exe.

