Layout facts for the synthetic TEB, PEB, loader lists and KUSER_SHARED_DATA
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

src/win.rs tags each field it writes with where its offset comes from. No text
is copied; these are the sources of the facts, all Microsoft documentation
under the CC BY 4.0 notice above:

  [pe]  PE Format specification, "The .tls Section" (TEB+0x2C TLS array)
        MicrosoftDocs/win32, desktop-src/Debug/pe-format.md,
        commit 8a9c5d8f32001411f5e572a17e6d736d6fcc055f
  [dbg] Debugger documentation, `dt` output from 32-bit Windows: TEB NtTib
        (0x00), ClientId (0x20), ThreadLocalStoragePointer (0x2C),
        ProcessEnvironmentBlock (0x30); PEB Ldr (0x0C); PEB_LDR_DATA Length
        (0x28), Initialized (0x04) and its three list heads (0x0C, 0x14, 0x1C).
        MicrosoftDocs/windows-driver-docs, commit
        6de78e042e0eaba466569c7f5ed65c250c644a0b: debugger/
        debugging-a-stack-overflow.md, debuggercmds/dt--display-type-.md,
        debuggercmds/c---numbers-and-operators.md
  [wtl] winternl.h reference: LDR_DATA_TABLE_ENTRY (InMemoryOrderLinks 0x08,
        DllBase 0x18, FullDllName 0x24, and the positions of the reserved
        slots at 0x00, 0x10, 0x1C and 0x2C), MicrosoftDocs/sdk-api (commit
        above), ns-winternl-peb_ldr_data.md
  [kus] KUSER_SHARED_DATA reference: field order only,
        MicrosoftDocs/windows-driver-docs-ddi (commit above),
        ns-ntddk-kuser_shared_data.md

Fields tagged [obs] are not given by these sources. Each holds a value a
32-bit Windows process can compare against an API that reports the same thing,
which is how the offset is established:

  TEB 0x00/0x04/0x08   ExceptionList, StackBase, StackLimit: the SEH chain
                       head and the stack bounds of the running thread
  TEB 0x18             Self: equals the TEB address
  TEB 0x20/0x24        GetCurrentProcessId(), GetCurrentThreadId()
  PEB 0x08             GetModuleHandle(NULL)
  PEB 0x18             GetProcessHeap()
  PEB 0x64             GetSystemInfo().dwNumberOfProcessors
  PEB 0x68             global flags as set with gflags for the image
  PEB 0xA4..0xB0       RtlGetVersion(): major, minor, build, platform id
  LDR entry 0x00/0x10  walking the load-order and initialisation-order lists
                       reaches the same entries the memory-order list does
  LDR entry 0x1C/0x20  the module's entry point and SizeOfImage from its headers
  LDR entry 0x2C       the module's file name
  KUSER 0x00..0x270    GetTickCount(), the system time, the system root and
                       RtlGetVersion() major/minor
